what is opportunity how do you have a  good opportunity versus bad opportunity  i see it as three variables so you have  the total number of potential units to  sell how many units of this widget could  i potentially sell number one number two  is what is the value to cost discrepancy  so how much profit can i potentially  make solving this particular problem and  then number three is what are the  competitive dynamics within that  marketplace so  uh an example that has two of the three  would be like what if i wanted to sell  cell phone service  lots of people need it  the how much it cost me to add an  additional customer is very very low so  very high gross margins but what are the  competitive dynamics well there's a lot  of really entrenched players it's very  hard to get into that right and so when  i'm looking at an opportunity i want to  see all three the difficulty with using  those three is that that equation can  evolve over time and so if you're  starting a business right now you might  not have you know sell something that  everyone in the world can buy but as you  get into business you learn more  and then you realize that you can expand  your market in one way or another
 

